-- Widget-type upgrade pass on marketplace attribute_schema content: converts
-- free-text/plain-number fields to select/multiselect/stepper wherever a
-- genuinely bounded real-world vocabulary exists (Vehicle Brand, laptop
-- Storage Type & Size, pet/livestock Age, small bounded quantities, ...),
-- for a better picker-driven UX and homogeneous, filterable data. Only the
-- 26 subcategories that actually changed are touched here; everything else
-- keeps its content from 20270151000000_marketplace_attribute_schemas.sql
-- unchanged. Same dual-shape convention: "fields" for the mobile client,
-- "required"/"properties"/"additionalProperties" for
-- backend/internal/marketplace/attrs_validation.go. See
-- docs/adr/ADR-PR-marketplace-attribute-schema-enrichment.md.
--
-- Additive-only: UPDATEs the JSONB column on existing rows, no DDL.
-- Idempotent: unconditional UPDATE keyed by (market_id, slug).

